  "title": "IEEE 802.11: Fix dissection of Wi-Fi Alliance vendor IEs",
  "description": "The tvb passed to dissect_vendor_ie_wfa does not include the OUI\nat the beginning. ieee80211_tag_vendor_specific_ie has already\nadvanced the offset past the OUI and shortened the tag len to\naccount for that. The first octet is the vendor type. This behavior\nwas changed in 2cbe215f2fd0263893c84634b00eed374abad5c3 but while\nother vendors were previously passed in the entire tvb plus an\noffset of 3, skipping past the OUI, the Wi-Fi Alliance vendor\nspecific function did not have an offset passed in, and started\nits offset at zero and skipped past the OUI itself. Thus its\nfunction required slightly different changes than other dissectors.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
